  "request": {
    "spec": "A person's grade is now dated. The person form gains a from-date (default the sheet's today), and\neach save with a grade records that grade from that date, keeping the ones already recorded; the first\ngrade a person was given applies from the beginning of time. A claim uses the grade in force on\nthe claim's date to find its rate; the list shows the grade in force on the sheet's today, and\nPERSON_EDITED carries that same grade, the one in force on the sheet's today after the save (so a\ngrade dated from another day may leave both unchanged). An import line gives its grade from the\nsheet's today.\n",
    "prompt": "You are implementing ONE change to this application.\n\nFIRST read AGENTS.md \u2014 it states the working rules and how the app is tested, and sends you to\nDESIGN.md for the app's stack and conventions. Follow both.\n\nTHE CHANGE REQUEST:\nA person's grade is now dated. The person form gains a from-date (default the sheet's today), and\neach save with a grade records that grade from that date, keeping the ones already recorded; the first\ngrade a person was given applies from the beginning of time. A claim uses the grade in force on\nthe claim's date to find its rate; the list shows the grade in force on the sheet's today, and\nPERSON_EDITED carries that same grade, the one in force on the sheet's today after the save (so a\ngrade dated from another day may leave both unchanged). An import line gives its grade from the\nsheet's today.\n\nYour work is verified by an automated Playwright UI test already installed under e2e/specs/.\nRead that spec: it declares the exact data-testid anchors, values, test data and any audit\nrecords it expects \u2014 match them. Run `bin/e2e` to build the app, start it, and run the test as\nyou work; iterate until it passes. Change whatever the request needs across the app \u2014 its stored\ndata, its server and its front end. Do NOT edit bin/build, bin/start, bin/stop, bin/e2e,\nAGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, DESIGN.md, e2e/support/ or the test spec.\n"
  },
